# Four-ply info spelling: April 2006 UCI specification, info and Move format
# https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/#engine-info and fisher-8hc question 1
# (order of fields approved by the owner 2026-11-24; these sessions staged
# 2026-11-24 and awaiting the owner's approval). D3–D6 supply the
# allowances for the principal variation, time and nodes per second. The fisher-2aj.2 sources and
# comments below supply the retained scores, node counts and reply order.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and fisher-l7f owner decisions from 2026-11-22.
# Search: fisher-2aj rules 1 to 7 and 10. Exact search values
# were checked by exhaustive enumeration with python-chess 1.11.2.
# Starting score: four-ply minimax with python-chess 1.11.2 followed rules
# 1 to 7. An independent reviewer reproduced cp 0 and per-ply counts
# 20/400/8902/197281 with their own minimax. See expectations/perft.epd.
# Searched transcript written 2026-11-23.
# UCI position and move format. e5d6 is en passant, and e1g1 castles.
> position startpos moves e2e4 a7a6 e4e5 d7d5 e5d6 e7e6 g1f3 g8f6 f1e2 f8e7 e1g1
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes; time, nps and pv as in the header.
< info depth 4 score {score} time {time} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} pv {pv}
# UCI bestmove. The reply carries a legal move in the current position.
< bestmove {legal}
# UCI position and move format. The castling rook leaves the h-file.
> position fen 8/6k1/6B1/3B4/5Q2/8/6R1/4K2R w K - 0 1 moves e1g1
> go
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. Black must play g7h8, then f4f8 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 64, 58 and 3599 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate -1 time {time} nodes 3722 nps {nps} pv {pv}
# The only legal reply fails if the castling rook still attacks h8.
< bestmove g7h8
# UCI position. The en passant capture makes d5 available to the black king.
> position fen 8/8/5B2/3pP1K1/4k3/8/5Q2/4N3 w - d6 0 1 moves e5d6
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes; time, nps and pv as in the header.
# If pinned, the expected value is cp -2400 nodes 7199. The second review
# reproduced it with a shakmaty 0.30.3 minimax (per-ply counts 1/40/177/6981).
< info depth 4 score {score} time {time} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} pv {pv}
# The only legal reply fails if the captured pawn stays on d5.
< bestmove e4d5
# UCI position and move format. The pawn promotes to a knight.
> position fen 3Q4/P7/k7/3K4/8/1R6/8/8 w - - 0 1 moves a7a8n
> go
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. Black must play a6a7, then d8a5 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 39, 48 and 1923 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate -1 time {time} nodes 2011 nps {nps} pv {pv}
# The only legal reply fails if the promotion creates a queen.
< bestmove a6a7
# The next move requires a knight on a8. A bishop cannot reach b6.
> position fen 3Q4/P7/k7/3K4/8/1R6/8/8 w - - 0 1 moves a7a8n a6a7 a8b6
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes; time, nps and pv as in the header.
< info depth 4 score {score} time {time} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} pv {pv}
# Black can play either a7a6 or a7b7 after the full replay.
< bestmove {legal}
> position fen 8/P7/8/8/8/6q1/5k2/7K w - - 0 1
> go
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. White must promote on a8, then g3h3 is checkmate after any promotion.
# Python-chess counts 4, 102, 848 and 20013 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate -1 time {time} nodes 20967 nps {nps} pv {pv}
# UCI move format and bestmove. Every legal move has a promotion suffix.
< bestmove {legal}
> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# The owner accepts an empty moves list as zero moves in fisher-l7f.7.
> position startpos moves
> go
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. Published perft counts sum to 206603. See the header for cp 0.
< info depth 4 score cp 0 time {time} nodes 206603 nps {nps} pv {pv}
# The starting position replaces the prior position, whose only move is h8g8.
< bestmove {legal}
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1 moves
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8h7, then g5g7 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 25, 45 and 1228 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate -1 time {time} nodes 1299 nps {nps} pv {pv}
# The owner accepts an empty list after FEN too. This position has one legal move.
< bestmove h8h7
> position startpos
> go
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. Published perft counts sum to 206603. See the header for cp 0.
< info depth 4 score cp 0 time {time} nodes 206603 nps {nps} pv {pv}
# The starting position replaces the prior position, whose only move is h8h7.
< bestmove {legal}
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
